_id\": \"qb-97d009ad2ae19a0d7d1db25c\", \"level\": \"high-school\", \"question_type\": \"bonuses\", \"source\": \"2022 IQBT Regular Season Set 1\", \"round\": \"10\", \"number\": \"11\", \"parts\": [{\"label\": \"L\", \"question\": \"The 1987 Montreal Protocol banned this general class of chemical compounds. For 10 points each:\", \"answer\": \"\"}, {\"label\": \"A\", \"question\": \"Name these compounds utilized as refrigerants, propellants, and solvents, that react in the  atmosphere to create radicals.\", \"answer\": \"CFCs [or chlorofluorocarbons]\"}, {\"label\": \"B\", \"question\": \"CFCs were the chief contributor to the depletion of this triatomic oxygen molecule.\", \"answer\": \"ozone [prompt on O3]\"}, {\"label\": \"C\", \"question\": \"The absorption of ultraviolet light by the ozone layer causes this phenomenon in the stratosphere, in  which the usual relationship between altitude and another property changes direction.\", \"answer\": \"temperature inversion\"}]}]}}",
